B.ajC=new A.b9(B.akk,["A dog is a friendly animal that many people keep as a pet.","A cat is a small furry pet that says 'meow' and likes to nap.","A bird is an animal with feathers and wings that can fly and sing.","A fish is an animal that lives in water and breathes through gills.","A butterfly is an insect with big colorful wings that flies from flower to flower.","A horse is a large strong animal that people can ride.","A chicken is a farm bird that lays eggs and says 'cluck'.","A pig is a pink farm animal that likes to roll in the mud.","A cow is a big farm animal that gives us milk and says 'moo'.","A frog is a small green animal that jumps and lives near water.","An elephant is a huge gray animal with big ears and a long trunk.","A rabbit is a small soft animal with long ears that hops.","Red is the bright color of apples, tomatoes, and fire trucks.","Blue is the color of the clear sky and the deep sea.","Yellow is the bright color of the sun and bananas.","Green is the color of grass, leaves, and many plants.","Orange is the color you get by mixing red and yellow, like a carrot.","Purple is the color made by mixing red and blue, like grapes.","A circle is a round shape with no corners, like a wheel.","A square is a shape with four equal sides and four corners.","A triangle is a shape with three straight sides and three corners.","A star is a shape with five points, like the ones in the night sky.","A heart is a shape we use to show love.","White is the color of clouds, milk, and fresh snow.","A flower is the colorful, sweet-smelling part of a plant.","One is the first counting number, written as 1.","Two is the number that comes after one, written as 2.","Three is the number that comes after two, written as 3.","Four is the number that comes after three, written as 4.","Five is the number of fingers on one hand, written as 5.","Six is the number that comes after five, written as 6.","Seven is the number of days in a week, written as 7.","Eight is the number that comes after seven, written as 8.","Nine is the number that comes after eight, written as 9.","Ten is the number of fingers on both hands, written as 10.","Twenty is two groups of ten, written as 20.","A hundred is ten groups of ten, written as 100.","The head is the top part of your body where your face is.","Eyes are the parts of your face that you use to see.","Ears are the parts of your body that you use to hear.","The nose is the part of your face you use to smell and breathe.","The mouth is the part of your face you use to eat and talk.","Hands are the parts at the ends of your arms that hold things.","Feet are the parts at the ends of your legs that you stand on.","Fingers are the long parts of your hand that grab and point.","Hair is the soft strands that grow on top of your head.","Teeth are the hard white parts in your mouth used to chew.","Shoulders are where your arms join the top of your body.","Knees are the parts in the middle of your legs that bend.","Rice is small white grains that many people eat as a meal.","Water is the clear drink we need every day to stay healthy.","Bread is a soft food made from flour that we bake and eat.","Milk is a white drink from cows that helps bones grow strong.","An apple is a round, crunchy fruit that can be red, green, or yellow.","A banana is a long, curved yellow fruit that is soft and sweet.","An egg is an oval food from chickens that we cook and eat.","Chicken is the meat from a chicken that people cook and eat.","Juice is a sweet drink made by squeezing fruit.","Vegetables are healthy plant foods like carrots, beans, and spinach.","Soup is a warm liquid food made by cooking things in water.","Candy is a small sweet treat made mostly of sugar.","A bottle is a container with a narrow top that holds drinks.","A cup is a small open container that you drink from.","A spoon is a tool with a small bowl shape for eating soup and rice.","A fork is a tool with pointed prongs for picking up food.","A plate is a flat dish that you put your food on.","A mother is a woman who has a child and cares for the family.","A father is a man who has a child and cares for the family.","A brother is a boy who has the same parents as you.","A sister is a girl who has the same parents as you.","A grandmother is the mother of your mother or father.","A grandfather is the father of your mother or father.","'Hello' is a friendly word you say when you greet someone.","'Thank you' is what you say to show you are grateful.","'Please' is a polite word you use when you ask for something.","'Sorry' is what you say when you feel bad about a mistake.","'Good morning' is a greeting you say early in the day.","A friend is someone you like and enjoy spending time with.","A t-shirt is a light shirt with short sleeves you pull over your head.","Pants are clothes that cover each leg from your waist to your ankles.","A dress is a one-piece outfit, often worn by girls and women.","Socks are soft clothes you wear on your feet inside your shoes.","Shoes are what you wear on your feet to protect them when you walk.","A cap is a soft hat with a brim that shades your eyes from the sun.","A jacket is warm clothing you wear over your shirt when it is cold.","A uniform is the special set of clothes you wear to school or a job.","Shorts are short pants that end above the knees for hot days.","Gloves are clothes you wear on your hands to keep them warm or safe.","Glasses are lenses you wear over your eyes to help you see clearly.","A backpack is a bag you carry on your back to hold your things.","Sunny means the sky is clear and the sun is shining brightly.","Rainy means water is falling from the clouds as rain.","Cloudy means the sky is covered with gray clouds.","A rainbow is a colorful arc of light in the sky after the rain.","A storm is rough weather with strong wind, heavy rain, and thunder.","Windy means the air is moving fast and blowing things around.","Hot means the weather is very warm and makes you sweat.","Cold means the weather is chilly and makes you shiver.","A flood is when too much water covers land that is usually dry.","Lightning is a bright flash of electricity in the sky during a storm.","Partly cloudy means there are some clouds and some sunshine.","Night is the dark part of the day when the sun is down.","A book is pages joined together that you read to learn or enjoy.","A pencil is a thin tool you use to write or draw, and you can erase it.","A notebook is a book of blank pages where you write your notes.","A crayon is a colored wax stick you use to color pictures.","A ruler is a straight tool you use to measure and draw straight lines.","Scissors are a tool with two blades that you use to cut paper.","A pen is a tool with ink that you use to write.","Paint is colored liquid you brush on to make pictures.","An eraser is a soft tool you use to rub out pencil marks.","A chair is a seat with a back where one person sits.","A school is a place where children go to learn.","A teacher is a person whose job is to help students learn.","A table is a piece of furniture with a flat top and legs.","Paper is a thin flat material that you write, draw, or print on.","A ball is a round object that you throw, kick, or bounce in games.","A door is the part of a room you open and close to go in or out.","A window is an opening in a wall with glass that lets in light.","A television is a screen that shows moving pictures and sound.","A phone is a device you use to call and talk to people far away.","A car is a vehicle with four wheels that people drive on roads.","A bus is a long vehicle that carries many people at once.","A bicycle is a two-wheeled ride you move by pushing the pedals.","An airplane is a vehicle with wings that flies people through the sky.","A ship is a very large boat that carries people or goods across the sea.","A train is a line of cars that runs on tracks and carries many people.","A motorcycle is a fast two-wheeled vehicle with an engine.","A helicopter is a flying machine with spinning blades on top.","A taxi is a car you pay to drive you where you want to go.","A boat is a vehicle that floats and carries people on water.","To walk is to move on your feet, step by step.","A road is a hard path that cars and people travel on.","Happy is the good feeling you have when you are glad and smiling.","Sad is the down feeling you have when something makes you unhappy.","Angry is the strong feeling you have when something upsets you.","Scared is the feeling you have when something frightens you.","Surprised is the feeling you get when something unexpected happens.","Loved is the warm feeling of knowing people care about you.","Sleepy is the feeling of being tired and ready to sleep.","Sick is the feeling of being unwell in your body.","Proud is the happy feeling you get when you do something well.","Confused is the feeling of not understanding something.","Excited is the bubbly feeling of really looking forward to something.","Calm is the peaceful, relaxed feeling of being quiet inside.","Monday is the first day of the school week.","Tuesday is the day that comes after Monday.","Wednesday is the day in the middle of the week.","Thursday is the day that comes after Wednesday.","Friday is the last day of the school week.","Saturday is a weekend day when there is no school.","Sunday is a weekend day for rest and family.","Morning is the early part of the day when the sun comes up.","Afternoon is the part of the day after noon and before evening.","Evening is the part of the day when the sun goes down.","A clock is a device that shows you what time it is.","Today is this day, the one that is happening right now.","To run is to move very fast using your legs.","To walk is to move by putting one foot in front of the other.","To jump is to push yourself up into the air with your legs.","To eat is to put food in your mouth and swallow it.","To drink is to take water or juice into your mouth.","To sleep is to close your eyes and rest your whole body.","To read is to look at words and understand what they say.","To write is to make letters and words with a pen or pencil.","To sing is to make music with your voice.","To dance is to move your body to music.","To clap is to hit your hands together to make a sound.","To sit is to rest your body on a chair or the floor.","To stand is to be up on your feet.","To open is to move something so it is no longer closed.","To close is to shut something so nothing can pass through.","To wave is to move your hand to say hello or goodbye.","To cry is to have tears fall from your eyes when you are sad.","To laugh is to make a happy sound when something is funny.","To swim is to move through the water with your body.","To play is to have fun with games or toys."],t.l)
